1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
In the last five years of HSC Chemistry

2
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:05,760
and Biology papers, one key word came up

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,560
in the written section more than any other:

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:09,600
explain.

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,360
Fifty-seven question parts, more than twice as many

6
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,320
as the next word.

7
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,160
Most were worth two to four marks.

8
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:20,880
And every year, NESA's marking feedback mentions answers

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,760
that say what happens, but not why.

10
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,400
So let's sort out three verbs that look

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,880
alike, but ask for different things.

12
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,980
Here's what NESA's glossary says, in short.

13
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,300
Identify means recognise and name.

14
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:40,100
Describe means give the features or characteristics.

15
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,900
In plain words: what it's like, or what

16
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:43,460
happened.

17
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,300
Explain means show the cause and effect: how

18
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,660
or why it happens.

19
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:51,940
A fourth verb, outline, asks for the main

20
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,300
features in general terms, a lighter describe.

21
00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:57,860
NESA also says to read each verb in

22
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:00,100
its question, so let's use one.

23
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,300
Here's an HSC-style question.

24
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,380
In fruit flies, eye colour depends on a

25
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,180
gene on the X chromosome.

26
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:11,380
A white-eyed female is crossed with a red-eyed

27
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:11,940
male.

28
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,780
Among the offspring, all 52 females have red

29
00:01:15,860 --> 00:01:19,580
eyes, and all 48 males have white eyes.

30
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,900
Part a asks you to identify, part b

31
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,780
to describe, and part c to explain.

32
00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:28,340
If you take Chemistry, you don't need the

33
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,580
fly details.

34
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:32,500
Watch what each verb makes the answer do.

35
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:36,900
Part a says identify, for one mark.

36
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:39,540
So the answer is a name: the red

37
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:40,900
allele is dominant.

38
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:41,860
That's it.

39
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:44,580
No reason is asked for, and a paragraph

40
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,660
here only takes time from the parts that

41
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:47,580
need it.

42
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,660
When identify is worth two marks, read the

43
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:54,020
question again: it may ask for two things.

44
00:01:55,234 --> 00:01:58,593
Part b says describe, for two marks.

45
00:01:58,914 --> 00:02:01,953
Describe means saying what happened, with the features

46
00:02:01,994 --> 00:02:02,513
that matter.

47
00:02:03,154 --> 00:02:06,513
All 52 female offspring had red eyes, and

48
00:02:06,674 --> 00:02:09,273
all 48 males had white eyes.

49
00:02:09,554 --> 00:02:12,273
In other words, every daughter had her father's

50
00:02:12,354 --> 00:02:14,913
eye colour, and every son had his mother's.

51
00:02:15,714 --> 00:02:18,673
Use the numbers, and notice what's missing: there's

52
00:02:18,754 --> 00:02:19,873
no "because".

53
00:02:20,354 --> 00:02:22,353
Describe doesn't ask why.

54
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:27,006
Part c says explain, for three marks, and

55
00:02:27,087 --> 00:02:29,726
it asks why the males and females differ.

56
00:02:30,287 --> 00:02:32,246
So now you need causes.

57
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:35,526
Three marks suggests about three linked points.

58
00:02:35,727 --> 00:02:37,486
And the content words tell you what to

59
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:41,406
explain: males all white, females all red.

60
00:02:41,807 --> 00:02:44,126
A good explanation accounts for both.

61
00:02:44,367 --> 00:02:46,846
There's no constraint phrase this time, so any

62
00:02:46,927 --> 00:02:49,406
correct reasoning about the chromosomes counts.

63
00:02:50,634 --> 00:02:51,993
Start from the cause.

64
00:02:52,274 --> 00:02:55,273
The eye-colour gene is on the X chromosome,

65
00:02:55,354 --> 00:02:57,353
and the Y has no copy of it.

66
00:02:57,674 --> 00:02:58,473
That's point one.

67
00:02:59,114 --> 00:03:01,033
A son gets his only X from his

68
00:03:01,194 --> 00:03:04,113
mother, and she has two white alleles.

69
00:03:04,394 --> 00:03:06,873
So every son has one white allele, with

70
00:03:06,954 --> 00:03:09,033
nothing to hide it, and he has white

71
00:03:09,114 --> 00:03:09,713
eyes.

72
00:03:09,914 --> 00:03:10,953
Point two.

73
00:03:11,034 --> 00:03:13,673
A daughter also gets her father's X, which

74
00:03:13,754 --> 00:03:15,353
carries the red allele.

75
00:03:15,434 --> 00:03:18,233
Red is dominant, so every daughter has red

76
00:03:18,314 --> 00:03:19,113
eyes.

77
00:03:19,234 --> 00:03:20,233
Point three.

78
00:03:20,354 --> 00:03:22,633
Each point says what causes what.

79
00:03:23,834 --> 00:03:25,593
Now here's a weaker answer.

80
00:03:26,234 --> 00:03:28,313
"All the males had white eyes and all

81
00:03:28,394 --> 00:03:30,953
the females had red eyes, because the trait

82
00:03:31,034 --> 00:03:34,153
is sex-linked and males have only one X."

83
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:36,953
The first half just repeats part b.

84
00:03:37,514 --> 00:03:40,233
Then it never says how it works: where

85
00:03:40,354 --> 00:03:42,633
each X comes from, for sons or for

86
00:03:42,714 --> 00:03:43,273
daughters.

87
00:03:43,994 --> 00:03:45,833
In our marking guide it earns one of

88
00:03:45,994 --> 00:03:49,273
three, for saying males have only one X.

89
00:03:49,514 --> 00:03:52,073
It described when the question said explain.

90
00:03:52,714 --> 00:03:54,953
Notice it even says because.

91
00:03:55,354 --> 00:03:58,073
A because isn't enough: it has to say

92
00:03:58,234 --> 00:03:58,873
how.

93
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,140
The same ladder works in Chemistry.

94
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,660
Take the iron tube from the last video.

95
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:08,180
Identify the colour after the crystals dissolve: deeper

96
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:08,820
red.

97
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:12,180
Describe what happens: the pale red solution turns

98
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:14,580
a deeper red as the crystals dissolve.

99
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:17,860
Explain it: with more iron three plus ions,

100
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:20,740
they meet thiocyanate ions more often, so the

101
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:23,460
forward rate rises above the reverse, and more

102
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,140
of the red ion forms.

103
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:27,300
Same tube, same chemistry.

104
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:29,940
Only the verb changed, and it changed what

105
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,060
earns the marks.

106
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,746
So here's a quick test.

107
00:04:34,027 --> 00:04:36,746
Read each sentence and ask: does it say

108
00:04:36,987 --> 00:04:38,506
what causes what?

109
00:04:38,827 --> 00:04:40,906
If it only says what happened, it's a

110
00:04:41,227 --> 00:04:42,826
description, however long it is.

111
00:04:43,467 --> 00:04:46,026
NESA's marking guidelines show the same step.

112
00:04:46,507 --> 00:04:49,466
In one recent three-mark explain question, about a

113
00:04:49,547 --> 00:04:53,866
disease-prevention campaign, outlining the campaign's features reached two

114
00:04:53,947 --> 00:04:57,546
marks, and only explaining its effect reached three.

115
00:04:58,267 --> 00:05:00,986
Explain questions run from two marks to seven.

116
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:04,066
More marks means a longer chain, not a

117
00:05:04,107 --> 00:05:04,986
longer list.

118
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:06,840
Your turn.

119
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:09,640
Do the one in your subject, or both.

120
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,080
Chemistry first.

121
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:13,640
A sealed bottle of soda water holds an

122
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:17,480
equilibrium between carbon dioxide gas and dissolved carbon

123
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,200
dioxide.

124
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:21,120
When the cap is removed, bubbles form in

125
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:21,880
the drink.

126
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,360
Explain why.

127
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:24,600
Three marks.

128
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,200
Pause here to answer.

129
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,960
Removing the cap lets carbon dioxide gas escape,

130
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,720
so there's less above the drink.

131
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:45,240
Fewer gas molecules dissolve, so the dissolving rate

132
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,800
falls, while leaving goes on at the same

133
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,160
rate, at first.

134
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:52,840
Leaving is now faster, so carbon dioxide comes

135
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,600
out of solution as bubbles.

136
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,400
A linked Le Chatelier answer works too.

137
00:05:57,960 --> 00:06:00,840
The habit to drop: "bubbles form because gas

138
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:03,560
comes out of the drink." That just describes

139
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,040
them.

140
00:06:05,267 --> 00:06:06,666
Now Biology.

141
00:06:06,947 --> 00:06:09,666
When a DNA molecule is copied, the two

142
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:12,226
new molecules are identical to each other.

143
00:06:12,707 --> 00:06:15,866
Assuming no copying errors, explain why.

144
00:06:16,147 --> 00:06:17,026
Two marks.

145
00:06:17,267 --> 00:06:18,706
Pause here to answer.

146
00:06:29,134 --> 00:06:31,533
Two marks, two linked points.

147
00:06:31,774 --> 00:06:34,893
The strands separate, and each original strand is

148
00:06:34,974 --> 00:06:36,613
a template for a new one.

149
00:06:36,894 --> 00:06:40,573
Nucleotides join by complementary base pairing, A with

150
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:43,533
T and C with G, so each new

151
00:06:43,614 --> 00:06:46,013
strand has the same sequence as the template's

152
00:06:46,094 --> 00:06:49,053
old partner, and both molecules get the original

153
00:06:49,134 --> 00:06:50,053
sequence.

154
00:06:50,414 --> 00:06:52,893
The habit to drop: "each has one old

155
00:06:52,974 --> 00:06:55,773
strand and one new strand." That says how

156
00:06:55,854 --> 00:06:58,573
they're built, not why the sequences match.

157
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,080
So, when you see the verb: identify, name

158
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,280
what the question asks for, and use the

159
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,760
marks to check how many.

160
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:10,440
Describe, give the features, with numbers if there's

161
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:11,000
data.

162
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:14,040
Outline, the main features, briefly.

163
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,400
Explain, show how each cause leads to its

164
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,680
effect, step by step, and check every sentence

165
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:22,640
says what causes what.

166
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,360
Next: compare and contrast, where the trick is

167
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,800
writing in pairs.

168
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,440
Here are the key notes.

169
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,600
Pause the video if you need more time

170
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,480
to copy them.
